# File: scripts/__tests__/features/sdlc-models.feature
# Generated from: specs/535-make-sdlc-execute-stage-models-and-efforts-configurable-per-project-via-steering-sdlc-models-json/requirements.md
Feature: Per-project execute stage models and efforts

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Onboarding creates the stage model file with defaults
    Given a project without steering/sdlc-models.json
    When the onboard plan runs "sdlc-models.mjs ensure --root ."
    Then steering/sdlc-models.json contains version 1 and model and effort entries for start, implement, verify, deliver, and repair with the plugin defaults

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Plugin defaults match today except verify effort
    Given the plugin default table
    When the defaults are read
    Then start is haiku/default, implement is haiku/xhigh, verify is opus/high, deliver is haiku/xhigh, and repair is opus/default

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Upgrade creates or completes the file and preserves project values
    Given a project whose steering/sdlc-models.json sets verify to sonnet/max and lacks repair and deliver.effort
    When the upgrade plan applies the sdlc-models item
    Then repair and deliver.effort gain default values, verify stays sonnet/max, and a second detection reports no sdlc-models item

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Stage workers use project values
    Given steering/sdlc-models.json sets verify to model sonnet and effort max
    When execute dispatches the verify worker
    Then the worker argv contains "--model sonnet --effort max"

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Repair re-dispatch uses the project repair entry
    Given steering/sdlc-models.json sets repair to model opus and effort high
    When a repairable failure triggers the next verify dispatch
    Then that worker argv contains "--model opus --effort high" and the dispatch after the stage passes uses the verify entry

  @SCN006
  Scenario: A missing file falls back to defaults with one warning
    Given a project without steering/sdlc-models.json
    When execute dispatches its stages
    Then every worker argv uses the plugin defaults and the controller output contains the missing-file warning exactly once

  @SCN007
  Scenario: nmg-router model ids pass through verbatim
    Given steering/sdlc-models.json sets implement to model "opencode-go/kimi-k3.1-pro" with effort xhigh
    When execute dispatches the implement worker
    Then the worker argv contains "--model opencode-go/kimi-k3.1-pro --effort xhigh"

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Invalid configuration fails closed before any external call
    Given steering/sdlc-models.json sets verify effort to "extreme"
    When execute starts
    Then it exits with status 2, prints a diagnostic naming steering/sdlc-models.json, "verify.effort", and "extreme", and makes no Herdr, Git, or GitHub call

  @SCN009
  Scenario: The supervisor model check is unaffected
    Given steering/sdlc-models.json configures every stage model
    When execute checks the session model
    Then executeModelRefusal returns the same result as without the file
